un green.\nABLATION (breadcrumb causation). Mutation and restore both proven on disk, and the tree was REBUILT on each leg. Target content/docs/data-modeling/meta.json; HEAD blob hash captured first and non-empty; trap '<restore>' EXIT INT TERM with an absolute repo root. Mutation: deleted-text count went 1 -> 0 and hash-object moved 25bf32b7 -> 0a2e03a6 (so the edit landed; not the editor's exit code). Rebuilt with next build (exit 0) and restarted next start, then read the RENDERED page: /docs/data-modeling/objects went from 'ObjectStack > Documentation > Object Metadata' (3 crumbs) to 'ObjectStack > Documentation > Data Modeling(/docs/data-modeling) > Object Metadata' (4). Control /docs/ai/agents, whose meta.json was untouched, stayed at 3 — so the effect is the line, not the rebuild. Restore leg: git checkout HEAD -- <path>, then git diff HEAD empty, git status clean, and hash-object back to 25bf32b7 == the HEAD blob; the tree was then rebuilt clean before any further measurement, so no later reading came off the mutated build. Predicted direction before running: the ablated section's trails lengthen while the control stays short — observed exactly that.\nEARLIER INSTRUMENTED BUILD, same discipline: a temporary console.warn probe in docsTrail (hash f444e51d, restored to 0c9be673 == HEAD blob, probe grep count back to 0) printed the raw fumadocs return: getBreadcrumbItems('/docs/data-modeling/objects') = [{\"name\":\"Data Modeling\"},{\"name\":\"Object Metadata\",\"url\":\"/docs/data-modeling/objects\"}] — the ancestor has a name and no url. That is the measurement behind the falsified assumption 2, not an inference from the tree's shape.\nVALIDATION METHOD — Google's Rich Results Test was NOT run and is not claimed: it is a hosted tool needing a public URL, and this branch is not deployed (#12333 also pins production to a pre-branch build). Instead, every JSON-LD block the site serves was checked field by field against schema.org property ranges and Google's documented required/recommended properties, over all 408 sitemap URLs: {\"pages\":408,\"withLd\":407,\"byType\":{\"Organization\":407,\"SoftwareSourceCode\":1,\"TechArticle\":403,\"BreadcrumbList\":403,\"BlogPosting\":3}}, failures: 0. Asserted per block: exactly one ld+json script; payload parses; @context is https://schema.org; NO raw '<' survives into the payload (the injection guard checked on output); every URL-valued property absolute and on https://objectstack.ai except the three declared external ones (sameAs, license, codeRepository); no relative URLs; every bare {\"@id\"} reference resolves inside that same page's @graph; Organization has name/url/logo/sameAs; TechArticle and BlogPosting have headline/image/author/publisher/mainEntityOfPage/url with url == the canonical and headline within Google's 110-char cap; datePublished and dateModified match ISO 8601; dateModified byte-equal to that page's <lastmod> in /sitemap.xml on all 406 dated pages (e.g. /docs/data-modeling/objects carries 2026-08-25T16:30:09.000Z in both); BreadcrumbList positions contiguous from 1, every entry with a name and an absolute item, last entry the page itself; SoftwareSourceCode.license is the Apache-2.0 URL rather than the bare SPDX id, because schema.org's license ranges over CreativeWork|URL and not Text.\nBREADCRUMB POPULATION on the final build: 403 docs URLs, 231 complete trails, 172 short — short ones concentrated in ai 8, api 11, automation 9, capabilities 10, concepts 5, data-modeling 17, deployment 11, getting-started 8, kernel 22, permissions 20, plugins 4, protocol 24, releases 8, ui 15.\nVERBATIM EMITTED BLOCKS for one page of each type are in the PR body and reproduced in the report JSON below.",
